-- title:
--   Level-zero branch of the edge chart is a localised line
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal O$ be a commutative ring and $\pi\in\mathcal O$ an element whose principal ideal $(\pi)$ is maximal, let $r$ be a natural number with $1<r$, and let $i\in\mathrm{Fin}\,2$ be one of the two variable indices. Here `chartERing 𝒪 π r` is the localisation away from the element `edgeQuot.discr 𝒪 π r` (the class of `edgeDiscr 𝒪 r`) of the quotient of $\mathrm{MvPolynomial}\,(\mathrm{Fin}\,2)\,\mathcal O$ by the ideal generated by `edgeRel 𝒪 π`, and `chartERing.ofPoly` is the induced $\mathcal O$-algebra map from $\mathrm{MvPolynomial}\,(\mathrm{Fin}\,2)\,\mathcal O$ to it. The assertion is that there exists a ring isomorphism $e$ from the iterated quotient of `chartERing 𝒪 π r`, first by the ideal generated by $(\text{the image of }\pi)^{0+1}$ and then by the ideal generated by the class of `ofPoly (X i)`, onto the localisation of $k[X]$ away from $X^{r-1}-1$, where $k:=\mathcal O/(\pi^{0+1})$ and $k[X]$ is $\mathrm{MvPolynomial}\,\mathrm{Unit}\,k$, such that: for every $a\in\mathcal O$, $e$ sends the class of the image of $a$ to the image of $a\bmod \pi^{0+1}$ under the structure map; and $e$ sends the class of `ofPoly (X (1 - i))`, the other of the two variables, to the image of $X$.
--
--   This identifies each of the two branches of the level-zero (special) fibre of the standard edge chart in the Čerednik–Drinfeld formal model as a localised affine line over the residue ring $\mathcal O/(\pi)$, compatibly with the structure maps from $\mathcal O$. It is used to prove [`CerednikDrinfeld.FormalOmega.chartERing.smoothOfRelativeDimension_one_specMap_quotient_of_mem_minimalPrimes_level_zero`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.FormalOmega.chartERing.smoothOfRelativeDimension_one_specMap_quotient_of_mem_minimalPrimes_level_zero), the smoothness of relative dimension one of the components of that fibre.
-- source:
